    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b38c",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s387",
          "text": "• In ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s388",
          "text": "Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s389",
          "text": ", malpractice claims often require ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38a",
          "text": "expert testimony and a certificate of review",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38b",
          "text": ", while ordinary negligence claims usually do not.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b38g",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38d",
          "text": "• Examples of ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38e",
          "text": "ordinary negligence in medical settings",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38f",
          "text": " include hazards like wet floors, unsecured equipment, or unsafe walkways.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b38k",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38h",
          "text": "• Examples of ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38i",
          "text": "medical malpractice",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38j",
          "text": " include misdiagnosis, surgical errors, medication mistakes, and failure to properly monitor or treat a patient.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b38r",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l38m",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38l",
          "text": "Medical care rests on trust, and when that trust breaks, Colorado patients often struggle to tell whether harm came from simple carelessness or a deeper professional failure. At ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38n",
          "text": "Dormer Harpring",
          "marks": [
            "l38m",
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38o",
          "text": ", we regularly speak with people who believe a healthcare provider let them down, yet feel uncertain about how the law defines responsibility. Understanding ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38p",
          "text": "what is considered medical malpractice",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38q",
          "text": " versus general negligence helps injured patients see when Colorado law allows accountability for medical errors that never should have happened.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "image",
      "_key": "i38s",
      "src": "./images/2026-02-what-is-considered-medical-malpractice.jpg",
      "alt": "what is considered medical malpractice"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b38x",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l38u",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/denver-medical-malpractice-lawyer/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38t",
          "text": "Colorado draws this distinction deliberately because not every medical mistake carries the same legal weight. Negligence applies across everyday situations, while ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38v",
          "text": "medical malpractice",
          "marks": [
            "l38u"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38w",
          "text": " focuses on professional judgment inside healthcare. That difference shapes proof, deadlines, and potential recovery. Many patients sense something went wrong long before a provider acknowledges it, yet second-guess those instincts when explanations feel technical or dismissive. Clear guidance around responsibility helps patients regain footing early, while evidence and legal options remain available.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b38z",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s38y",
          "text": "What is Negligence?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b393",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l390",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/negligence"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s391",
          "text": "Negligence",
          "marks": [
            "l390"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s392",
          "text": " describes everyday carelessness, the kind that occurs when someone fails to act with reasonable caution in a situation where harm could have been avoided. Courts examine whether a person ignored a responsibility, acted without care, or failed to step in when caution was required. The focus stays on whether that conduct exposed others to unnecessary risk, not on intent or bad motives.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b398",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l395",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/contributory-negligence-vs-comparative-negligence/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s394",
          "text": "Across Colorado, ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s396",
          "text": "negligence claims",
          "marks": [
            "l395"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s397",
          "text": " arise in familiar places such as traffic crashes, unsafe buildings, and job sites where safety takes a back seat. The standard stays grounded in ordinary behavior rather than specialized training. Inside medical facilities, this distinction matters because some injuries stem from basic safety oversights rather than diagnosis or treatment.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39a",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s399",
          "text": "Examples of Negligence in Medical Settings",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39c",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39b",
          "text": "Some injuries occur in healthcare facilities without involving medical judgment at all. These situations often remain ordinary negligence claims, even when they occur inside hospitals or clinics.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39e",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39d",
          "text": "Examples include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39j",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l39g",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/types-of-slip-and-fall-accidents/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39f",
          "text": "A ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39h",
          "text": "patient slips on an unmarked wet floor",
          "marks": [
            "l39g"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39i",
          "text": " in a treatment area.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39l",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39k",
          "text": "Loose cords or equipment left in walkways causing a fall.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39n",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39m",
          "text": "Failure to secure a wheelchair or hospital bed properly.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39p",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39o",
          "text": "These incidents involve basic safety responsibilities similar to those of any other business. They do not require medical expertise to evaluate and typically fall outside professional malpractice claims under Colorado law.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39r",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39q",
          "text": "What is Medical Malpractice?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b39w",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l39t",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.coloradojudicial.gov/sites/default/files/2024-06/Chapter%2015_0.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39s",
          "text": "Medical malpractice goes beyond an unfortunate result or a treatment that did not work as hoped. It arises when a licensed healthcare provider makes a decision, or fails to act, in a way that falls outside accepted medical practice and causes real harm to a patient. In Colorado, courts assess this conduct by comparing it to how a reasonably careful provider in the same medical field would have handled the situation under similar circumstances. ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39u",
          "text": "Colorado’s civil jury instructions on professional negligence",
          "marks": [
            "l39t"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39v",
          "text": " frame this comparison by focusing on the conduct expected of similarly trained providers when diagnosing, treating, and monitoring patients under comparable circumstances.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3a0",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39x",
          "text": "This definition carries significant legal consequences. Medical malpractice claims operate under stricter procedural rules than ordinary negligence cases, including expert review requirements and statutory limits on certain damages. Understanding ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39y",
          "text": "what is considered medical malpractice",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s39z",
          "text": " requires recognizing when professional medical judgment, not general carelessness, sits at the center of the injury.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3a2",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3a1",
          "text": "Examples of Medical Malpractice",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3a4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3a3",
          "text": "Medical malpractice centers on decisions or omissions tied directly to patient care, diagnosis, or treatment. These cases require medical experts to evaluate whether a provider’s conduct fell below professional expectations.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3a6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3a5",
          "text": "Common examples include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3a8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3a7",
          "text": "Failure to diagnose or delayed diagnosis of a serious condition.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3aa",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3a9",
          "text": "Surgical errors involving improper technique or inadequate preparation.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ac",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ab",
          "text": "Medication mistakes caused by incorrect dosing or overlooked interactions.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ae",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ad",
          "text": "Ignoring symptoms that clearly warranted further testing or referral.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ag",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3af",
          "text": "Each example involves specialized medical judgment, which separates malpractice from routine negligence and defines how courts evaluate professional medical errors in Colorado.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ai",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ah",
          "text": "Key Differences: Negligence vs. Malpractice",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ak",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3aj",
          "text": "In Colorado, negligence and medical malpractice share a legal foundation yet operate under different rules. Negligence covers unreasonable conduct by anyone, while malpractice applies only to licensed medical professionals acting within their professional role.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ao",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3al",
          "text": "Medical malpractice carries additional safeguards because claims challenge clinical judgment rather than everyday conduct. Colorado law requires early expert support and limits certain damages, reflecting the seriousness of alleging professional medical failure. This framework explains why ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3am",
          "text": "what is considered medical malpractice",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3an",
          "text": " demands a higher level of proof than an ordinary negligence claim.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3aq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ap",
          "text": "Key differences include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3at",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ar",
          "text": "Who the standard applies to:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3as",
          "text": " Negligence applies broadly, while malpractice applies only to healthcare professionals.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3aw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3au",
          "text": "Standard of care:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3av",
          "text": " Negligence relies on reasonable behavior, while malpractice relies on professional medical standards.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3az",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ax",
          "text": "Expert testimony:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3ay",
          "text": " Malpractice requires qualified medical experts, while negligence often does not.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3b2",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3b0",
          "text": "Damage limitations:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3b1",
          "text": " Colorado caps non-economic damages in medical malpractice cases.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3b4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3b3",
          "text": "Misunderstanding these differences can carry real consequences. When an injury gets labeled incorrectly, critical deadlines or procedural requirements may surface too late, placing otherwise valid claims at risk.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3b6",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3b5",
          "text": "Similarities of Negligence and Malpractice",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3b8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3b7",
          "text": "Despite procedural differences, negligence and malpractice share core legal elements. Both require proof of duty, breach, causation, and damages. Both focus on whether the conduct caused real harm, not simply an unfavorable outcome.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3ba",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3b9",
          "text": "Colorado courts evaluate these claims with the same underlying purpose: compensating injured individuals while discouraging unsafe conduct. Medical settings often blur the line between professional judgment and basic safety responsibilities, which explains why patients frequently struggle to understand how courts classify these cases.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3bc",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3bb",
          "text": "Legal Implications of Negligence vs. Malpractice",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3be",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3bd",
          "text": "The legal consequences of classifying a claim as malpractice extend far beyond terminology. Medical malpractice cases require a certificate of review confirming expert support, compliance with specific filing rules, and adherence to statutory damage caps. Courts enforce these requirements strictly, and procedural missteps can derail otherwise strong claims.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b3bi",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3bf",
          "text": "Negligence cases outside malpractice avoid many of these hurdles. This distinction affects strategy, cost, and timing from the earliest stages of a case. Knowing ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3bg",
          "text": "what is considered medical malpractice",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s3bh",
          "text": " helps injured patients pursue accountability without unnecessary delays or avoidable procedural barriers.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
